    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 full suite: **34 run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule. The tier is fixed at create time (mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` pattern), so \"after this create\" semantics are preserved:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persistent `householdMemberCount` field (`@Column(name = \"household_member_count\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 on create, computes and stores the household member count: the existing owners sharing the same normalized last name + address, plus the owner being created. Uses the same case-insensitive / whitespace-collapsed normalization that derives `householdId`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier`** \u2014 returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`; otherwise falls through to the existing SILVER (namesakeCount 0 + email present) and BRONZE rules.\n\n4. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column, and updated the positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` rows in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the only seed file using positional inserts) to include the extra value.\n\nThe new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD for a 3-member household) passes, and the existing tier/household/namesake tests (Cp11, Cp13, Cp15) remain green.",
